Dodgin' Diamond II game for OS/2, release 0.2.2 beta
This is a little shoot'em up arcade game for one or two players.

You should install some dll (and related dependencies), this is the complete 
list of all packages containing all main dynamic libs (dll) you should 
have to play Dodgin' Diamond II release 0.2.2. beta on OS/2:

ftp://ftp.netlabs.org/pub/gcc/gcc4core-1_3_1.wpi (*.dll)
ftp://ftp.netlabs.org/pub/gcc/libc-0.6.6-csd6.zip (*.dll)
http://hobbes.nmsu.edu/download/pub/os2/dev/SDL-1.2.15-20160303.zip (*.dll)

To install as user, usually executables and libs should be respectively somewhere 
in path and in libpath statements, unzip and enjoy!

For netlabs.org's yum/rpm system, simply check for:

yum install libc libgcc1 libgcc-fwd libstdc++6 libsupc++6

to install all main necessary packages 

See also the author's README file included.

More info and sources are available at:
https://www.usebox.net/jjm/dd2/
